    {
      "id": "gL3rZqqCGXSyCaLF81NkZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 414.71508788476564,
      "y": 493.10427122222245,
      "width": 557.9396362304688,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#e9ecef",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1791113769,
      "version": 927,
      "versionNonce": 1177175047,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792507624523,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Ticket (cuda-oxide: \"witness\") = proof this thread\npassed col < width.\n\nIt holds the thread's own (row, col); no two threads get\nthe same one.\n\nget_mut only takes a ticket, so a thread\ncan only write to its own spot. \n\nindex_2d_runtime makes sure that the thread's col is \nin range, then get_mut takes that ticket, linearizes its\n(row, col) find its spot in memory, and we write there.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Ticket (cuda-oxide: \"witness\") = proof this thread\npassed col < width.\n\nIt holds the thread's own (row, col); no two threads get\nthe same one.\n\nget_mut only takes a ticket, so a thread\ncan only write to its own spot. \n\nindex_2d_runtime makes sure that the thread's col is \nin range, then get_mut takes that ticket, linearizes its\n(row, col) find its spot in memory, and we write there.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
